WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.519
So this next story started to develop last
night.

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:27.340
And I have to tell you, I can't wait.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.869
I am really like a kid on Christmas morning
and I'm Jewish.

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:36.270
But the metaphor just works like a kid on
Christmas morning waiting for video to be

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.390
released because Donald Trump yesterday was
interviewed for an upcoming episode of 60

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.390
Minutes.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.290
And we've learned that in the middle of the
interview, Trump abruptly and furiously got

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.910
up and left, ending the interview with 60
Minutes correspondent Lesley Stahl and then

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:55.579
started tweeting ridiculous things about the
interview.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:57.789
This has to be seen to be believed.

00:00:57.789 --> 00:01:04.030
The reporting is that in the interview, Trump
became frustrated with the questions that

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.840
Leslie Stall was asking.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.880
That tracks perfectly with Trump's displeasure
at being asked real questions and in particular,

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.700
in situations where he can't weasel his way
out.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:19.560
The example from last week's town hall where
Savannah Guthrie actually pressed Trump about

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.000
his obvious lies as to when was he tested?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.250
Was he tested for Corona virus before the
debate?

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.960
And Trump was obviously lying and being dishonest.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.990
And Trump lost it on Savannah Guthrie, saying
she was terrible, horrible, all this stuff.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:36.620
Same thing happened with 60 Minutes after
about 45 minutes of the 60 Minutes interview.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.770
Trump gets up and leaves and just doesn't
come back.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.600
But he was highly, highly triggered first.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.610
Trump tweeted a video of the interviewer,
Leslie Stall, not wearing a mask at the White

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:48.420
House as an attack on her.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:53.090
We later learned that this was just moments
after Trump abruptly left the interview.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.719
And Leslie Stall, of course, being on camera,
had removed her mask.

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:00.000
And she was talking to producers about like
it's Trump coming backers.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.210
Is this over?

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:03.119
She hadn't yet put her mask on.

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:04.450
Trump attacking her for that.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.450
That's already weird.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:10.250
But then Trump bizarrely tweeting about the
interview itself, that, quote, I am pleased

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:14.890
to inform you that for the sake of accuracy
in reporting, I am considering posting my

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.890
interview with Leslie Stahl of 60 Minutes
prior to airtime.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:22.630
This will be done so that everybody can get
a glimpse of what a fake and biased interview

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.040
is all about.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:29.450
Everyone should compare this terrible electoral
intrusion with the recent interviews of sleepy

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:30.450
Joe Biden.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:36.220
So I guess the implication is maybe Trump
has the raw video of the entire interview.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.650
Or maybe Trump's just lying.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.910
Who the hell knows?

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:45.680
But apparently a reporter asking real questions
is considered an intrusion on the electoral

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.680
process.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.600
Now, per Donald Trump, this is a joke, guys.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.600
We are a joke.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.600
The country is a joke.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.600
This man is a joke.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.660
It really can't continue.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:03:00.660
And in normal situations, a president being
unable to handle a 60 Minutes interview, walking

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.660
out.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.049
It would be a national scandal if Barack Obama
had done this.

00:03:06.049 --> 00:03:10.359
It would be 24/7 on right wing news saying
the president can't handle it.

00:03:10.359 --> 00:03:11.440
What an embarrassment.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.710
He can't stand the heat.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:17.190
If he can't stand up to Leslie Stall, how
can he stand up to Xi and Putin and Kim Jong?

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.190
Right.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:21.030
All that stuff, if it had been Obama with
Trump.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:26.949
Trump has so weaponized his followers against
the media in a dystopian act of hostility

00:03:26.949 --> 00:03:28.790
that the Trump ists are furious.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:33.979
If you look at the places online where the
trump is hang out, the Trump ists are furious

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:36.769
with Leslie Stall and with 60 Minutes.

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:42.970
But what we can be sure of is that if Trump
walked out, the interview must have been really

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:48.010
bad, because even interviews that you and
I recognize as having gone badly for Donald

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.010
Trump.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.049
Trump thinks he did well.

00:03:50.049 --> 00:03:55.709
So if even Trump thinks he didn't do well
in the interview, it must be a complete disaster

00:03:55.709 --> 00:04:01.090
if Trump flees the interview and starts slamming
the interviewer on Twitter.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.360
You know, it went really, really bad.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.250
And I hope that this is released Sunday.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:07.080
Very much looking forward to it.

